      "side": 1,
      "message": "A few thoughts here:\n\n1) We\u0027re trying to test the VCN API (not the lower level APIs like the NetworkAgent API). Tests should test one thing, and writing tests that are as clean as possible (which this facilitates) is a win. We also shouldn\u0027t reinvent the wheel.\n\n2) Currently, there are CTS tests in the mainline module which are testing public API behavior for APIs not in the module (e.g. IPsec). If that\u0027s a reasonable dependency between the platform code and the Connectivity module, then some improvements to the TestNetworkService seem like they should be a totally reasonable dependency.\n\n3) Ben believes that in addition to these points, it\u0027s actually technically necessary to use TestNetworkService due to permissions restrictions, which is what required him to write it in the first place (https://android-review.googlesource.com/c/platform/frameworks/base/+/826957), and he\u0027ll provide that detail in a follow-up comment.",
